    "https://charleston.edu/academic-affairs/faculty-administration-manual/index.php": {
      "title": "Faculty/Administration Manual",
      "description": "College of Charleston | Faculty/Administration Manual Return to College of Charleston homepage MyPortal The Hub Alumni Give Visit Apply What're you looking for? What're you looking for? Search About College of Charleston About College of Charleston Home College at a Glance History & Traditions Looking to the Future Leadership & Administration Offices Facilities Community Academics Academics Home Find Your Program Meta-Majors Colleges & Schools Centers & Institutes Study Abroad & International Ed Research Opportunities Academic Resources & Services Online Degrees Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Home Tuition & Fees Apply for Aid Loans Scholarships Grants Pay Your Bill Student Life Student Life Home Housing & Dining Athletics Activities Calendar Clubs & Organizations Support & Services Service & Leadership Campus Resources Life in Charleston Admission Admission Home Apply Visit the College Parents & Families Admitted Students Request Information MyPortal The Hub Alumni Give Visit Apply Faculty/Administration Manual Faculty/Administration Manual August 2026 This is the official copy of the 2026-2027 Faculty/Administration Manual, for use until the next published version, anticipated August 2027. All editions of the Faculty/Administration Manual published, printed, or reproduced prior to this edition date should be discarded. Reference should be made only to the most recent edition of the Faculty/Administration Manual. The Faculty/Administration Manual link is available only at the following URL: https://charleston.edu/academic-affairs/documents/fam/fam-current.pdf. The Faculty/Administration Manual should not be archived or reproduced at any other URL without the express written consent of the Provost or President. The language used in the Faculty/Administration Manual does not create an employment contract between the employee and the agency. This document does not create any contractual rights or entitlements. The agency reserves the right to revise the content of this document, in whole or in part. No promises or assurances, whether written or oral, which are contrary to or inconsistent with the terms of the Faculty/Administration Manual create any contract of employment or contractual rights or entitlements. Executive Vice President for Academic Affairs and Provost Table of Contents Statement On Changes To The Faculty/Administration Manual Faculty Organization And By-Laws Preamble Article 1. Membership in the College Faculty Article 2. College Faculty Meetings Article 3. Officers Article 4. Faculty Senate Article 5. Committees Article 6. Meetings Held Electronically Article 7. Amending Procedures 1. The College Of Charleston A. Approved College History B. Accreditation C. Statement of Institutional Purpose (Mission Statement) 2. Administrative Organization A. Board of Trustees B. Description of the Administrative Organization of the College and Duties of its Officers C. The Deans of the Schools D. The Academic Department Chair E. Organization and Operation of the Faculty F. Institutional Committees 3. Faculty Appointments A. The Instructional Faculty B. Joint Appointments to the Instructional Faculty C. Instructional Faculty Appointments Outside Academic Departments D. Library Faculty E. Courtesy Faculty Appointments F. Emeriti Faculty Appointments 4. Conduct Of Faculty And Administrators A. Prohibition of Discrimination and Harassment B. Code of Professional Conduct and Statement of Professional Ethics C. Statement of Academic Freedom D. Consensual Relations Policy 5. Terms And Records Of Faculty And Unclassified Administrator Appointments A. The College Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Policies, Regulations and Procedures B. Contracts of Untenured Faculty and Unclassified Academic Administrators C. Faculty and Unclassified Administrator Records D. Probationary Appointments for Tenure-track Faculty and Instructors E. Adjunct Faculty Appointments F. Unclassified Administrators G. Terms of Instructional Faculty Employment and Workload H. Policy Concerning Outside Employment of Faculty I. Nepotism Policy J. Workload Policies of Schools K. Modification of Duties Procedure 6. Evaluation Of Faculty A. Third-year Review, Tenure and Promotion of Tenure-Track and Tenured Instructional Faculty B. Third-Year Review and Promotion of Instructors and Renewal of Senior Instructors C. Third-Year Review, Tenure and Promotion of the Library Faculty D. Procedures for Third-Year Evaluation, Tenure and Promotion of Instructional and Library Faculty E. Procedures for the Annual Evaluation of Instructional and Library Faculty F. Merit Raises G. Tenure-Clock Modification Policy H. Post-Tenure Review I. Review for Honorary Rank of University Professor or University Librarian IV 7. Faculty Discipline, Misconduct, And Termination A. Policy Governing Termination B. Discipline of Faculty Members C. Termination of Tenured Faculty Members “For Cause” and Termination Procedure D. Reduction In Force as it Applies to Faculty Members and Unclassified Administrators E. Policy For Misconduct In Research and Scholarship F. Procedures for Misconduct in Research and Scholarship 8. Faculty Interaction With Students A. Faculty Responsibilities to Students B. Students Grievances Procedures C. S tudents with Disabilities 9. Faculty Awards A. Distinguished Teaching Award B. Distinguished Adjunct Faculty Teaching Award C. Distinguished Research Award D. Distinguished Service Award E. Distinguished Advising Award F. William V. Moore Distinguished Teacher/Scholar Award G. Distinguished Undergraduate Mentoring Award H. Innovation in Teaching Award 10. Selected Administrative Policies For Faculty A. Faculty Leave Policies B. Faculty Research and Development C. Policy Affecting Travel and Entertainment by Faculty and Academic Staff D. Policy on Reimbursement for Approved Expenditures by Faculty Members and Administrative Officers E. Purchases by Faculty and Staff F. Legal Assistance G. Faculty and Administrator’s Authority to Enter into Contractual Agreements on Behalf of the College of Charleston H. Intellectual Property Policy I. Grievances Before the Faculty Hearing Committee In This Section Statement On Changes To The Faculty/Administration Manual Faculty Organization And By-Laws 1. The College Of Charleston 2. Administrative Organization 3. Faculty Appointments 4. Conduct Of Faculty And Administrators 5. Terms And Records Of Faculty And Unclassified Administrator Appointments 6. Evaluation Of Faculty 7. Faculty Discipline, Misconduct, And Termination 8. Faculty Interaction With Students 9. Faculty Awards 10. Selected Administrative Policies For Faculty Quick Links Academic Affairs' Hub Page Apply Now Visit Us Request Info Library Bookstore Alumni Give Directory Newsroom Events Careers Campus Map Emergency Info 66 George Street, Charleston, SC 29424 USA\n\t\t\t\t| 843.805.5507 Policies & Procedures Title IX Accessibility Transparency Copyright © 2026 College of Charleston. All Rights Reserved."
